title: diffsitter — Tree-sitter based AST difftool for semantic diffs
authors: Afnan Enayet
year: 2020–present
venue: Open source tool, GitHub
quality: CODE
url: https://github.com/afnanenayet/diffsitter
keywords: diffsitter, tree-sitter, AST diff, LCS, Rust, semantic diff, leaf matching
cites: []
cited_by: []
content:
  LANGUAGE: Rust. MSRV 1.85.1, edition 2024.
  APPROACH: Computes diff on AST of file rather than text.
    Uses tree-sitter parsers for parsing.
    MATCHING: Applies longest-common-subsequence (LCS) on syntax tree LEAVES
      (not internal nodes). This differs from GumTree (full subtree) and difftastic (graph search).
  GRAMMARS: Either compiled statically into binary, or loaded as dynamic libraries
    (libtree-sitter-{lang}.{ext}).
  FEATURE: Includes MCP server exposing tree-sitter AST navigation as tools for AI coding assistants.
  BUILD: Requires Rust toolchain + C99+/C++14+ compilers (for tree-sitter grammars) + git submodules.
  LIMITATION: LCS on leaves does not capture structural moves or renames.
  CARGO.TOML: https://github.com/afnanenayet/diffsitter/blob/main/Cargo.toml
<<<END>>>

