title: Common Threads in Incremental Data Flow Analysis: A Comprehensive Survey
authors: (authors not confirmed — search result only showed ACM URL)
year: 2024 (approx)
venue: ACM Computing Surveys. DOI: 10.1145/3768155
quality: PEER-REVIEWED
url: https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3768155
keywords: incremental dataflow, survey, IDFA, demand-driven, worklist, change propagation, recomputation
cites: Ryder-Paull 1988, numerous IDFA papers
cited_by: []
content:
  COVERAGE: Survey of incremental dataflow analysis techniques.
  KEY DISTINCTIONS:
    - Incremental analysis: updates analysis results based on prior computed facts.
    - Demand-driven analysis: computes only what is queried; does not use prior results.
    - Combined: incremental + demand-driven (e.g., incremental points-to via Datalog).
  CLASSIFICATION:
    - Pure incremental: Ryder-Paull-style worklist propagation from changed nodes.
    - Change-based: track edit deltas (inserted/deleted/modified nodes) explicitly.
    - Snapshot-based: compare two independent full analyses; report diffs.
  NOTE: Paper behind ACM paywall; full details not retrieved (403 on fetch attempt).
  RELEVANCE: Comprehensive reference for choosing incremental strategy in pflow diff.
<<<END>>>

SOURCE
id: 12
ts: 2026-05-29T00:00:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: Infer Differential Mode (infer reportdiff)
authors: Facebook / Meta (Infer team)
year: 2016–present
venue: Official documentation
quality: DOCS
url: https://fbinfer.com/docs/steps-for-ci/
keywords: Infer, differential analysis, reportdiff, --reactive, --changed-files-index, introduced.json, fixed.json, CI integration
cites: []
cited_by: []
content:
  WORKFLOW:
    Step 1 (feature branch): infer capture -- <build-cmd>
    Step 2 (main branch): infer capture --reactive --mark-if-unchanged -- <build-cmd>
      --reactive: prevents deletion of infer-out/; enables incremental analysis.
      --mark-if-unchanged: marks files that haven't changed to skip re-analysis.
    Step 3: Get changed files:
      git diff --name-only origin/feature..origin/main > index.txt
    Step 4: infer analyze --changed-files-index index.txt
      Analyzes only modified files + their direct dependents.
    Step 5: infer analyze --incremental-analysis --changed-files-index index.txt
      Incremental mode: further restricts to changed procedures.
    Step 6: infer reportdiff --report-current report-feature.json
                             --report-previous infer-out/report.json
  OUTPUT (infer-out/differential/):
    introduced.json: bugs found in feature branch NOT in main.
    fixed.json: bugs in main NOT in feature branch.
    preexisting.json: bugs in both branches.
  CONFIG: .inferconfig — JSON config file; INFER_ARGS env var overrides .inferconfig;
    command line options override INFER_ARGS.
  KEY DESIGN: Compares bug REPORTS between versions (not raw analysis facts).
    Does not directly expose CFG/PDG deltas — only bug-level diffs.
  RELEVANCE: Model for pflow diff output: report "introduced paths/edges" vs
    "fixed paths/edges" vs "preexisting" analogously.
<<<END>>>

