id: 13
ts: 2026-05-29T00:00:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: CodeQL Incremental Security Analysis for Pull Requests
authors: GitHub Security Lab
year: 2025
venue: GitHub Changelog, May 28 2025
quality: INDUSTRY
url: https://github.blog/changelog/2025-05-28-incremental-security-analysis-makes-codeql-up-to-20-faster-in-pull-requests/
keywords: CodeQL, diff-informed, incremental analysis, pull request, changed lines, database caching, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, Python, Ruby
cites: []
cited_by: []
content:
  PERFORMANCE: Up to 20% faster overall. JavaScript/TypeScript scans most impacted: up to 58% faster.
  MECHANISM: "Only analyzes new or changed code" rather than scanning entire codebase.
    Generates a CodeQL database representing new/changed code.
    Combines it with a cached database for entire codebase.
  DIFF-INFORMED ANALYSIS (earlier feature, now incremental):
    Retrieves changes between base and head branches.
    Calculates line ranges that were added or modified.
    Creates a CodeQL extension pack for focused analysis.
    Configures queries to prioritize results in changed code.
  API BEHAVIOR CHANGE: When using code scanning API with `pr` query parameter,
    now "only returns new alerts found within the changed code."
    Previously: returned all codebase alerts, filtered downstream.
  SUPPORTED LANGUAGES (incremental): JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, Ruby, Python.
    Future expansion planned.
  AVAILABILITY: Default-on at github.com as of May 28, 2025.
    CodeQL CLI support coming later.
    GitHub Enterprise Server: starting with version 3.19.
  RELATED: GitHub Changelog 2026-03-24 "Faster incremental analysis with CodeQL in pull requests":
    https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-24-faster-incremental-analysis-with-codeql-in-pull-requests/
  RELEVANCE: Shows production approach — incremental DB + cache + diff-range filtering.
<<<END>>>

