id: 16
ts: 2026-05-29T00:01:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: SymDiff — Language-Agnostic Semantic Diff Tool for Imperative Programs
authors: Shuvendu K. Lahiri, Chris Hawblitzel, Ming Kawaguchi, Henrique Rebelo
year: 2012
venue: CAV 2012 (International Conference on Computer Aided Verification). Springer LNCS 7358, pp. 567–574.
quality: PEER-REVIEWED
url: https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/paper-44.pdf
keywords: SymDiff, semantic diff, Boogie, equivalence checking, behavioral difference, SMT, counterexample, language-agnostic
cites: Boogie, Z3 SMT solver
cited_by: []
content:
  APPROACH: Equivalence checking + semantic (behavioral) differencing.
    Operates on Boogie intermediate verification language (IVL).
    Source language translations exist for: C, C#, x86, others.
  
  SEMANTIC EQUIVALENCE DEFINITION:
    Two procedures P and P' are semantically equivalent iff for ALL inputs,
    they produce the same outputs and have the same termination behavior.
  
  ALGORITHM:
    1. Translate P and P' to Boogie IVL.
    2. Create a "product program" that runs both in lockstep.
    3. Use SMT solver (Z3) to check if product program can reach a state where outputs differ.
    4. If SAT: extract concrete counterexample (witness input showing behavioral difference).
       If UNSAT: programs are semantically equivalent.
  
  OUTPUT: If behavioral difference found:
    - Concrete input values demonstrating the difference.
    - Corresponding execution paths highlighted in source code.
  
  LOCKSTEP PRODUCT PROGRAM: For procedures P1 and P2 with shared variables:
    Rename variables: x → x1 (from P1), x → x2 (from P2).
    Assert: inputs are equal (x1_init = x2_init).
    Check: ∃ path where output1 ≠ output2.
  
  LIMITATIONS: Requires translation to Boogie (non-trivial for Python/JS).
    Bounded verification (may miss differences in unbounded loops).
    Expensive for large procedures (SMT solver invocation).
  
  RELEVANCE TO pflow diff: SymDiff represents the "semantic oracle" end of the spectrum.
    pflow diff at structural level (CFG/PDG deltas) vs SymDiff at semantic level
    (behavioral equivalence). Complementary approaches.
<<<END>>>

