content:
  NOTE: PDF binary — full content not extractable. Metadata from search snippets only.
  
  TOPIC: Interprocedural semantic change-impact analysis using equivalence relations.
  KEY CLAIM (from search snippet): "Equivalence relations can be leveraged to make
    dataflow-based CIA aware of the change semantics, thereby improving precision in the
    presence of semantics-preserving changes."
  
  CORE IDEA: Standard change impact analysis (CIA) is conservative: any textual change
    triggers impact propagation. If a change is semantics-preserving (e.g., refactoring),
    equivalence relations can prune false positives.
  
  APPLICATION: For pflow diff — distinguish "this change rewrote control flow but produced
    equivalent CFG paths" (no real delta) vs. "this change added a new path."
    arXiv URL for full paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.08734
