content:
  NOTE: Not fetched directly; metadata from search snippets only.
  TOPIC: Reuses computational history (function summaries) of previous program version.
    Summaries = over-approximations of bounded program behaviors.
    On change: "repair" summaries to maximize reusability for subsequent runs.
  APPROACH: Rather than recompute from scratch, repair the existing summary to
    account for the CFG delta introduced by the change.
  RELEVANCE: The "summary repair" pattern is an efficient alternative to full
    recomputation when diffs are small.
<<<END>>>

